{
  "id": "avoid-double-wrapping-polymorphic-model-serializers",
  "title": "Avoid double-wrapping polymorphic model serializers",
  "kind": "rule",
  "answers": [
    "Why are polymorphic model serializers wrapped twice?",
    "How should serializer construction return a resolved model serializer?",
    "How do I avoid adding a second polymorphism trampoline?"
  ],
  "body": "Symptom: Polymorphic model serializers are wrapped twice.\nRoot cause: The CombinedSerializer construction path called pydantic-core/src/serializers/shared.rs:CombinedSerializer::maybe_wrap_in_polymorphism_trampoline again after CombinedSerializer::find_serializer returned.\nFix pattern: Return CombinedSerializer::find_serializer's result directly from the final construction path instead of adding another trampoline wrapper.\nConstraints: Applies to this final serializer-resolution path; the diff does not establish that trampoline wrapping should be removed from other paths.",
  "applies": "Final serializer resolution in CombinedSerializer when constructing polymorphic model serializers.",
  "tags": [
    "serialization",
    "polymorphism",
    "model-serializers"
  ],
